<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ătīlĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Roman gentile name</i>, e. g. M. Atilius Regulus,
			Atilius Rufus, Atilius Verus, etc.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Atilia lex de dediticiis, <i>introduced by the tribune of the people L. Atilius</i>, A. U.
			C. 544, <i><span class="en">Liv. 26, 33</span></i> and
			34.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ătīlĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Atilius</i>, <i>Atilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus,</span>”
				<i>that of Atilius Regulus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 4, 4</span></i>
			, ext. 6.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
